{"name":"Pink Cattleya","hex":"#ffb2d0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"cattleya","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant of the genus Cattleya, a genus of orchids."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cattleya"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cattleya","blocks":[{"text":"Cattleya is a genus of orchids from Costa Rica south to Argentina. The genus is abbreviated C in trade journals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Cattleya_labiata_Orchi_1013.jpg/330px-Cattleya_labiata_Orchi_1013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cattleya","wikidata":"Q133733"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Cattleya_dowiana_var._aurea_%27Maestranza%27_%28Linden%29_B.S.Williams_%26_T.Moore%2C_Orchid_Album_2_t._84_%281883%29_%2848470977042%29.jpg/500px-Cattleya_dowiana_var._aurea_%27Maestranza%27_%28Linden%29_B.S.Williams_%26_T.Moore%2C_Orchid_Album_2_t._84_%281883%29_%2848470977042%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikiped